    "sha": "7d30af4bf79a6b813129e5ddc5f85ac2c19b338f",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVp7jidoAKDdkMzBhZjRiZjc5YTZiODEzMTI5ZTVkZGM1Zjg1YWMyYzE5YjMzOGY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "jnz-1",
        "email": "jnz-1@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T00:51:42Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "jnz-1",
        "email": "jnz-1@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T00:51:42Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(align): part alignment from two perpendicular edge picks (full 3D frame)\n\n#769: two perpendicular picks - an edge (or two points) for +Y and one\nfor +X - define the setup's part alignment outright, in full 3D.\npick::align_from_axes builds the frame with the primary axis kept\nexactly, the secondary orthogonalized against it (landing within the\nskew it came with), and +Z on the picks' cross (the right-hand rule),\nturning the part about the centre of its bounds; the origin is NOT set\nhere (the work offset stays where it is placed). A left-handed pair is\nhonoured literally instead of refused; only (nearly) parallel picks\nrefuse, by name. The landing is proved before the command stores\nanything. One picked axis keeps the in-plane turn (#557 unchanged).\nThe panel applies it (CommandKind renamed AlignPartFromAxes).\n\nTests: crates/app/tests/align_axes.rs (9) - the user's exact case\n(down-Z edge as +Y, -X edge as +X), part-on-its-side landing, subsumption\nof turn_in_plane for in-plane picks (pinned equal), single-pick\nfallback, skewed secondary within its skew, parallel refused by name,\nleft-handed honoured literally, compose-after-hold, face pick refused.\nUI: two_picks_with_an_upright_edge_align_the_part_in_full_3d (the\nround #557 refused, now aligning) + updated pins. Battery green:\nalign_axes 9, axis_align 10, plane_align 9, points_align 8,\nturn_pivot 5, ui setup_axis 9; clippy clean.\n\nFixes #769",
